      "original_statement": "The product vanishes exactly when a compatible extension diagram exists.",
      "proved_statement": "The fiber of Ext^1(Zprime,A) to Ext^1(B,A) over the first extension class is empty exactly when the product is nonzero; otherwise it is a torsor under Ext^1(C,A)/im(Hom(B,A) to Ext^1(C,A)).",
      "hypotheses": "An abelian category and the two specified short exact sequences. No enough-injective or enough-projective assumption.",
      "proof": {
        "file": "PROOFS_8774_9196.md",
        "bytes": 23554,
        "sha256": "5A5F788AF8D766E96EE44B82B27CB5BE2E9801331977297F5ABBBFB71CEA2CD6",
