      "status": "proved_editorial_consequence",
      "body_replacement": false,
      "novelty": "not_claimed",
      "limits": "Classifies middle-row extension classes admitting a compatibility isomorphism; it does not fix the isomorphism as part of the classification."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "DERIVED-UNDER-018",
      "source_lines": [
        9010,
        9050
      ],
      "original_statement": "All Ext^p(H^r K,H^s K) vanish for p>=2 and r>s.",
      "proved_statement": "Only Ext^(r-s+1)(H^r K,H^s K)=0 for r>s is needed for splitting. The actual truncation boundary is the precise stage obstruction. Identity-on-cohomology splittings form a torsor under 1+N, where N is the nilpotent ideal with entries Ext^(r-s)(H^r K,H^s K), r>s; when these entries vanish the splitting is unique.",
      "hypotheses": "K has bounded cohomology in an abelian category, with the displayed degree-specific vanishing for existence.",
      "proof": {
        "file": "PROOFS_8774_9196.md",
        "bytes": 23554,
        "sha256": "5A5F788AF8D766E96EE44B82B27CB5BE2E9801331977297F5ABBBFB71CEA2CD6",
